spl: sunxi: A733: load U-Boot proper from where binman puts it

binman places U-Boot proper (the FIT) at a fixed 0x4a000 after the SPL
on the A733 (min-size in sunxi-u-boot.dtsi, whose comment says it
matches SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_SECTOR). That sector was left at the
generic sunxi 0x40, so the SPL falls back to its own eGON length,
which is rounded up to 8 KiB: it reads U-Boot proper from 0x4a000 only
while the SPL is a bit larger than 0x48000. A smaller SPL reads 0xff
padding at 0x48000 and stops after "Trying to boot from MMC1".

Use 0x250 sectors (0x4a000) on the A733, the offset binman uses.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/common/spl/Kconfig
+++ b/common/spl/Kconfig
@@ -582,6 +582,7 @@
 config SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_SECTOR
 	hex "Address on the MMC to load U-Boot from"
 	depends on SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_USE_SECTOR
+	default 0x250 if MACH_SUN60I_A733
 	default 0x40 if ARCH_SUNXI
 	default 0x75 if ARCH_DAVINCI
 	default 0x8a if ARCH_MX6 || ARCH_MX7
